W: 1. Oh, my name is Jock Stewart. I'm a canny gaun man,
W: And a roving young fellow I've been.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: So be easy and free, when you're drinking with me.
W: I'm a man you don't meet every day.
W:
W: 2. I´m a roving young blade. I´m a piper to trade,
W: And there's many the tunes I can play.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 3. I have acres of land. I have men of command,
W: I have always a shilling to spare.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 4. Now, I took up my gun, and my dog I did hunt,
W: All down in the County Kildare.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 5. So, come fill up your glasses with brandy and wine.
W: Whatever it costs, I will pay.
W: (Chorus, 2x)
